A16_SMSS_72_M016936_037                                                       
                                                                              
Apollo 16 Soil Mechanics                                                      
Lunar Self-Recording Penetrometer (LSRP) Page C-4                             
                                                                              
Post Flight Calibration Table                                                 
                                                                              
This handwritten table gives the results of the postflight calibration        
tests of the Apollo 16 Lunar Self-Recording Penetrometer (LSRP) before        
it was washed with alcohol. The test used lunar drum S/N 2008 set to          
index 19. The calibration table was created at the University of              
California Soil Mechanics Laboratory and is dated 11-12 May 1972.             
                                                                              
The table columns give the drum load in degrees/minutes, the drum load        
in decimal degrees, the drum circumference deflection in millimeters,         
and the load in Newtons.  This gives the value for stress used on the         
plot. A second set of columns starts with a column labelled initial drum      
depth/final in cm and gives a running total of the drum reading.  The         
next column, delta Drum Depth Reading in cm gives the difference between      
the current drum depth reading and the initial value. The final column        
gives the actual penetration depth in cm.                                     
